# SyncSenta — Implementation Reference

*AI-readable knowledge document. Read before starting any session on this repo.
For the domain glossary, read CONTEXT.md first.*

---

## What SyncSenta is

SyncSenta (`studio/`) is an AI-powered Kenyan K–9 education platform.

- Students get an adaptive Socratic tutor, interactive CBC activities, and
  cross-device progress continuity
- Teachers get real-time analytics, CBC scheme-of-work and lesson plan
  generators, misconception detection, and intervention tools
- Deployed at: **sentastudio.vercel.app**
- Repo: **dgithinjibit/Ascendra** (monorepo)

---

## Current stack

```
Frontend:    Next.js 16 · React 18 · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS · shadcn/ui
Auth + DB:   Supabase (Postgres · RLS · Realtime · Storage)
LLM:         Groq llama-3.3-70b-versatile (switchable to Gemini via LLM_PROVIDER)
Session:     Upstash Redis — LearningSession per user, 7-day TTL
AI backend:  FastAPI (Python 3.11) on Render — LangGraph + specialists
Adaptive:    Rust rust-core/ (built, not yet wired to prod)
             TypeScript port in lib/omega-agent/metta-core.ts is the active engine
Deploy:      Vercel (Studio) + Render (AI Agents)
```

---

## Monorepo map

```
studio/          Primary Next.js application (this is where most work happens)
ai-agents/       FastAPI service — teacher generators, orchestrator
