## The Omega tutoring engine

The most important AI component. Runs on every `/api/chat` call (socratic mode).

**TypeScript implementation:** `lib/omega-agent/metta-core.ts`
**Rust source of truth:** `rust-core/src/agent_runtime.rs` (`decide_tutoring()`)
**Thresholds must stay in sync between the two.**

```
LearningState { attempts, correctAttempts, hintsUsed, frustrationSignal }
  ↓
evaluateTutoringDecision()
  frustrated || hintsUsed >= 2 || masteryPct < 40  →  Intensive
  attempts === 0 || masteryPct < 80                →  Guided
  else                                             →  Independent
  ↓
TutoringDecision { scaffolding, hint, nextAction }
  ↓
buildDynamicSystemPrompt()  →  system prompt with scaffolding instructions
  ↓
Groq / Gemini streaming call
  ↓
fire-and-forget: Redis LearningSession.preferences.scaffoldingLevel
```

The Rust service (`rust-service/`, port 8091) can replace the TS engine when
`SYNCSENTA_RUST_ADAPTIVE_URL` is set. Not yet in production.

---

## Subject session flow (shipped Sept 2026)

Ten subjects in `SUBJECT_REGISTRY` (`lib/subject-session.ts`):

- Core (sandbox layout): mathematics, english, kiswahili, environmental,
  creative, cre, indigenous
- Extended (chat layout): blockchain, financial-literacy, ai

All ten route through `/student/subject/[slug]`:
```
sandbox/page.tsx → openSubject() → /student/subject/[slug]/page.tsx
  parallel fetch:
    getSubjectXP()              → point_transactions
    /api/session/sync           → Redis resume point
    getOrCreateChatSession()    → chat_sessions
    getChatMessages(40)         → chat_messages
  chat layout → SubjectChat (full-height SSE, no toggle)
  sandbox layout → redirect to /student/sandbox/[grade]/[slug]
```

---

## Two curriculum data systems

These are different and serve different consumers — do not confuse them.

**`src/curriculum/`** (40 flat files, grade1–6, PP1–2)
- Powers the student sandbox activity catalogue
- Imported by `lib/curriculum-activities-mapper.ts` → `lib/sandbox-activities.ts`
- Contains activity question data

**`src/data/curriculum/`** (structured subdirs, PP1–Grade 9 + Junior Secondary)
- Powers teacher tools (scheme wizard, lesson planner, assessment generator)
- Imported via `src/data/curriculum/index.ts` → `getHardcodedStrands()`, `getSubjectsForGrade()`
- Contains CBC strand/substrand/learning outcome data

---

## Key Supabase tables

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `profiles` | User accounts — role, grade, classroom_id, language_preference |
| `chat_sessions` | Subject chat sessions — user_id, subject, grade, mode, status |
| `chat_messages` | Individual messages — session_id, role, content |
| `learning_progress` | Per-student per-subject mastery — questions_answered, correct_answers, mastery_level |
| `point_transactions` | XP per competency_code — drives subject level calculation |
| `behavioral_profiles` | Telemetry from canvas activities |
| `misconceptions` | Detected learning gaps |
| `interventions` | Teacher intervention records |
| `schemes` | Generated scheme-of-work documents |
| `lesson_plans` | Generated lesson plans |
| `exams` | Generated exams + student responses |
| `api_usage` | LLM call logging |

---

## What's NOT in production yet

- Rust adaptive service (built, env var not set in Vercel)
- Parent portal (no pages built yet)
- Real-time teacher WebSocket alerts (code exists in ai-agents, not fully wired)
- ESP32 firmware integration (API contract mismatch)
- Distributed rate limiting via Upstash on all routes (only `/api/chat` has it)

